# 🎯 Phase 8: Hub-Spoke Optimization Strategy
## AsyncSystem + DistributedSystem Integration

**Date**: 2026-03-15
**Current Performance**: 50K tasks/sec + 1K ops/sec
**Target Performance**: 60K tasks/sec + 1.5K ops/sec
**Improvement Target**: +20-50% throughput, 5ms → 1ms latency

---

## 📊 Current Architecture Analysis

### Async System Current State
```
AsyncSystem (50K tasks/sec):
├─ Task Scheduler: Vec-based dequeue (O(n) on remove)
├─ Ready Queue: FIFO (front removal penalty)
├─ Suspended Queue: Linear search for removal
├─ No work-stealing between queues
├─ Wakeup events: Vec append (unbounded growth)
└─ Task storage: HashMap lookup per poll
```

**Bottlenecks Identified**:
1. **Line 167** (task_scheduler.rs): `remove(0)` = O(n) array shift
2. **Line 181** (task_scheduler.rs): Linear search in suspended_queue
3. **Line 303** (task_scheduler.rs): Unbounded wakeup_events vector
4. **Line 200** (task_scheduler.rs): HashMap collision chains

### Distributed System Current State
```
DistributedSystem (1K ops/sec):
├─ Replication: One-entry-at-a-time (slow)
├─ Log matching: Linear scan for conflicts
├─ CommitIndex: Quorum check per entry
└─ No batching of AppendEntries
```

**Bottlenecks Identified**:
1. **Line 91-103** (raft_replication.fl): Serial entry processing
2. **Line 81-82** (raft_replication.fl): Linear backtracking on conflict
3. **Line 192-210** (raft_replication.fl): N² quorum checks
4. No network message batching

---

## 🔧 Phase 8 Optimization Plan

### Module 1: Async System - Work-Stealing Event Loop (200 lines)

**File**: `src/event_loop_pooling.rs`

```rust
// ============================================================================
// Phase 8.1: Work-Stealing Event Loop Pooling
// Current: O(n) dequeue + unbounded events
// Target: O(1) dequeue + bounded ringbuffer events
// ============================================================================

use std::collections::VecDeque;
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};
use std::sync::Arc;

// Fixed-size ring buffer for wakeup events (1024 slots)
pub struct WakeupRing {
    ring: Vec<WakeupEvent>,
    head: AtomicUsize,
    tail: AtomicUsize,
    mask: usize,  // Capacity - 1 (for modulo via bitwise AND)
}

impl WakeupRing {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        let capacity = 1024;  // Power of 2
        Self {
            ring: vec![WakeupEvent::default(); capacity],
            head: AtomicUsize::new(0),
            tail: AtomicUsize::new(0),
            mask: capacity - 1,
        }
    }

    // O(1) push with overflow handling
    pub fn push(&self, event: WakeupEvent) -> bool {
        let tail = self.tail.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        let next_tail = (tail + 1) & self.mask;
        let head = self.head.load(Ordering::Acquire);

        if next_tail == head {
            // Ring full - discard oldest event
            self.head.store((head + 1) & self.mask, Ordering::Release);
        }

        // SAFETY: Index is always valid due to mask
        unsafe {
            *self.ring.get_unchecked_mut(tail) = event;
        }
        self.tail.store(next_tail, Ordering::Release);
        true
    }

    // O(1) pop
    pub fn pop(&self) -> Option<WakeupEvent> {
        let head = self.head.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        let tail = self.tail.load(Ordering::Acquire);

        if head == tail {
            return None;  // Empty
        }

        let event = unsafe {
            *self.ring.get_unchecked(head)
        };

        self.head.store((head + 1) & self.mask, Ordering::Release);
        Some(event)
    }

    pub fn len(&self) -> usize {
        let head = self.head.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        let tail = self.tail.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        (tail - head) & self.mask
    }
}

// VecDeque-based ready queue (O(1) operations at both ends)
pub struct OptimizedTaskQueue {
    ready_queue: VecDeque<u32>,
    suspended_map: std::collections::HashSet<u32>,  // Fast O(1) removal
}

impl OptimizedTaskQueue {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            ready_queue: VecDeque::with_capacity(1000),
            suspended_map: std::collections::HashSet::new(),
        }
    }

    // O(1) pop from front
    pub fn dequeue_ready(&mut self) -> Option<u32> {
        self.ready_queue.pop_front()
    }

    // O(1) push to back
    pub fn enqueue_ready(&mut self, task_id: u32) -> bool {
        if self.ready_queue.len() >= 10000 {
            return false;
        }
        self.ready_queue.push_back(task_id);
        true
    }

    // O(1) add to suspended set
    pub fn enqueue_suspended(&mut self, task_id: u32) -> bool {
        self.suspended_map.insert(task_id)
    }

    // O(1) remove from suspended set
    pub fn dequeue_suspended(&mut self, task_id: u32) -> bool {
        self.suspended_map.remove(&task_id)
    }

    pub fn ready_count(&self) -> usize {
        self.ready_queue.len()
    }

    pub fn suspended_count(&self) -> usize {
        self.suspended_map.len()
    }
}

// Event loop with work-stealing
pub struct EventLoopPool {
    queue: Arc<OptimizedTaskQueue>,
    wakeup_ring: Arc<WakeupRing>,
    task_count: AtomicUsize,
}

impl EventLoopPool {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            queue: Arc::new(OptimizedTaskQueue::new()),
            wakeup_ring: Arc::new(WakeupRing::new()),
            task_count: AtomicUsize::new(0),
        }
    }

    // Work-stealing: Try to steal from wakeup events first
    pub fn poll_next(&mut self) -> Option<u32> {
        // Priority 1: Wakeup events (hot path)
        if let Some(event) = self.wakeup_ring.pop() {
            // Task was woken up by event
            return Some(event.task_id);
        }

        // Priority 2: Ready queue
        self.queue.dequeue_ready()
    }

    // Batch emit wakeup events (for I/O completions)
    pub fn emit_batch(&self, events: &[WakeupEvent]) {
        for event in events {
            self.wakeup_ring.push(*event);
        }
    }

    pub fn task_count(&self) -> usize {
        self.task_count.load(Ordering::Relaxed)
    }
}

// ============================================================================
// Tests
// ============================================================================

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn test_wakeup_ring_o1_push_pop() {
        let ring = WakeupRing::new();

        // Push 100 events O(1) each
        for i in 0..100 {
            let event = WakeupEvent {
                event_id: i,
                task_id: i % 10,
                reason: WakeupReason::Timeout,
                timestamp: i as u64,
            };
            assert!(ring.push(event));
        }

        // Pop 100 events O(1) each
        for i in 0..100 {
            let event = ring.pop();
            assert!(event.is_some());
        }
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_optimized_queue_o1_operations() {
        let mut queue = OptimizedTaskQueue::new();

        // Enqueue 1000 tasks O(1) each
        for i in 0..1000 {
            assert!(queue.enqueue_ready(i));
        }
        assert_eq!(queue.ready_count(), 1000);

        // Dequeue 1000 tasks O(1) each
        for _ in 0..1000 {
            assert!(queue.dequeue_ready().is_some());
        }
        assert_eq!(queue.ready_count(), 0);
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_suspended_set_fast_lookup() {
        let mut queue = OptimizedTaskQueue::new();

        // Add to suspended set O(1)
        for i in 0..100 {
            assert!(queue.enqueue_suspended(i));
        }

        // Remove from suspended set O(1)
        for i in 0..100 {
            assert!(queue.dequeue_suspended(i));
        }
        assert_eq!(queue.suspended_count(), 0);
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_ring_overflow_graceful() {
        let ring = WakeupRing::new();

        // Fill ring completely
        for i in 0..1024 {
            let event = WakeupEvent {
                event_id: i,
                task_id: i % 10,
                reason: WakeupReason::IoReady,
                timestamp: i as u64,
            };
            ring.push(event);
        }

        // Overflow - should discard oldest
        let overflow = WakeupEvent {
            event_id: 9999,
